-- ============================================================================
-- Migration: Sheet Metal Lookup Tables -- combined export batch 2 (staging)
-- Purpose: Lands 8 more lookup tables (tblToolLife already staged separately
--          as migration 513, skipped here) into the same lossless staging
--          table earlier migrations created. See migration 479's header for
--          the staging/promotion architecture. Source name sanitized per
--          the standing rule against naming the licensed source.
--
--          Per-table consumer check (grepped the live cost-engine code
--          before staging, per this reconciliation's standing practice):
--
--          - tblRouterUtilities (8 rows, cutting speed/feed by material +
--            tool diameter): "2 Axis Router" has NO cost engine in this app
--            at all (confirmed repeatedly this session) -- no consumer.
--          - tblWaterjetAbrasiveNozzle (3 rows, nozzle cost + life in hours
--            by grade): this app's waterjet costing (waterjet-engine.ts)
--            amortizes ABRASIVE MATERIAL cost (consumable_prices table,
--            migration 362) but has NO nozzle-wear cost term at all -- a
--            real, distinct, currently-missing cost line item. NOT added
--            here -- adding a new cost term to a live formula is a real
--            product decision (changes every existing waterjet quote's
--            cost), not a data fix. Flagged for a decision, not built.
--          - tblWaterjetMachinabilityFactor (21 rows, material-cut-code-
--            family -> speed multiplier): this app's real
--            sm_lookup_waterjet_cut table (migration 398) already varies
--            cutting speed by material+thickness directly (not via a
--            separate multiplier layer) -- this export's material-cut-code
--            axis has no established mapping to this app's own material
--            classification, so it can't be safely cross-applied. Staged
--            for reference only.
--          - tblWaterjetCutGasRate (3 rows, Oxygen/Air/Nitrogen cost +
--            orifice life): despite the "WaterjetCut" file path, assist gas
--            is a LASER cutting concept (waterjet uses water+abrasive, not
--            process gas) -- likely the source tool's own folder
--            organization, not evidence this app's waterjet process needs a
--            gas cost term. No consumer either way.
--          - toolingHeatTreatCost / toolingHeatTreatCostMaterial (6+8 rows)
--            and tblToolLifeImprovementFactor (10 rows, coating type ->
--            tool life multiplier): all describe STAMPING TOOL fabrication
--            costs (build/harden/coat a die) -- this app does not build or
--            cost tooling at all (it costs the PART on an assumed-available
--            machine), so there is no live concept these could feed. No
--            consumer.
--          - validationDisplayControls (11 rows, panel name -> show/hide):
--            this is the SOURCE TOOL's own UI configuration (which of ITS
--            OWN panels are visible), not manufacturing data at all --
--            staged only for completeness/losslessness, explicitly not
--            manufacturing reference data.
